  <!--
    Encoding provenance (shared recipe for the CDNA1-4 legacy-math additions):

    LLVM public revision: 254f05a4807997ae410e157f1673c8c26020a88c
    https://github.com/llvm/llvm-project/commit/254f05a4807997ae410e157f1673c8c26020a88c
    llvm/lib/Target/AMDGPU/VOP1Instructions.td:
      V_EXP_LEGACY_F32 / V_LOG_LEGACY_F32 use VOP1_Real_vi 0x4b / 0x4c.
      VOP1_Real_e32e64_vi adds 0x140 for VOP3: 0x18b / 0x18c.
      VOP1_Real_vi also supplies the DPP and SDWA forms.
    Public byte vectors at that revision:
      llvm/test/MC/AMDGPU/gfx9_asm_vop1.s: V_EXP_LEGACY_F32 cases start at
      line 7615; V_LOG_LEGACY_F32 at 11710. These sections include e32,
      literal, DPP and SDWA forms (search the lowercase instruction names).
      llvm/test/MC/AMDGPU/gfx9_asm_vop3.s: e64 EXP starts at 29692,
      e64 LOG at 31240, including source and output modifiers.

    Base XML: ROCm/rocm-systems revision
      20acfc90b76ecae4cb5907a53bfa9bdb6b3f1904,
      shared/machine-readable-isa/isa/amdgpu_isa_cdnaN.xml, N = 1, 2, 3, 4.
    BaseArchitecture and BaseSchemaVersion copy ArchitectureName and
    Document/SchemaVersion. Id is the local unique label cdnaN-legacy-math.
    Each added instruction copies InstructionFlags and all
    InstructionEncodings/InstructionEncoding fields from V_EXP_F32 or
    V_LOG_F32 in that architecture's base XML, matched by EncodingName and
    EncodingCondition. This includes every Operand attribute, FieldName,
    DataFormatName, OperandType and OperandSize. Only InstructionName
    (insert _LEGACY) and Opcode change. Descriptions restate exp2/log2;
    they do not establish native rounding or approximation accuracy.

    Identifier derivation uses each base Encoding's BitCount, Radix and OP
    BitLayout. Copy the corresponding non-legacy identifier, clear OP,
    then insert the legacy opcode. ENC_VOP1 uses bits [16:9], giving
    0x7e009600 / 0x7e009800. VOP1_INST_LITERAL, VOP1_VOP_DPP and
    VOP1_VOP_SDWA use those same low words with a zero high word, as in
    the base identifiers; the base encoding conditions select extensions.
    ENC_VOP3 uses bits [25:16], giving 0x00000000d18b0000 /
    0x00000000d18c0000. Binary strings retain the base encoding width.
  -->
